---
kind: request
id: 01a041f7-f2ee-708a-a1d5-3b2ad4228e3e
name: ListStations
assertions:
- status: 200
- xpath: count(//*[local-name()='Station'])
  equals: '3'
- xpath: (//*[local-name()='Id'])[1]
  equals: NL-AMS-01
- xpath: (//*[local-name()='Station'])[1]/@kind
  equals: automatic
tags: [demo, soap]
---

```http
POST /demo/soap/weather.asmx
Content-Type: text/xml; charset=utf-8
SOAPAction: "http://demo.tap.dev/weather/ListStations"

<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/">
  <soap:Header>
    <wsse:Security soap:mustUnderstand="1" xmlns:wsse="http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-wssecurity-secext-1.0.xsd">
      <wsse:UsernameToken>
        <wsse:Username>{{wsseUsername}}</wsse:Username>
        <wsse:Password Type="http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-username-token-profile-1.0#PasswordText">{{wssePassword}}</wsse:Password>
      </wsse:UsernameToken>
    </wsse:Security>
  </soap:Header>
  <soap:Body>
    <ListStations xmlns="http://demo.tap.dev/weather">
      <Country>NL</Country>
    </ListStations>
  </soap:Body>
</soap:Envelope>
```

# ListStations

Every weather station in a country.

`Weather/WeatherSoap` · SOAP 1.1 · document/literal · action `http://demo.tap.dev/weather/ListStations`.

A repeating element in the response — `maxOccurs="unbounded"` on the WSDL side. The last
assertion reads an attribute, which XPath treats no differently from an element.
